Z||000003||Sndfr||12-04-2000||12:58 PM||||I'm talking about some tips on choosing.<P>Like:<BR>"Thin 5-spoke looks awesome."<BR>"Twenty little spokes is too ricey."<BR>"Seventeen inch rims are too big."<P>I'm lookin' for opinions now.<BR>(those examples aren't particularly <I>my</I> opinions)<P>------------------<BR>-<B>matthew "Whyt Nyte" d.</B><BR>84 SE<BR><I>"You are not special.<BR>You are not a beatiful and unique snowflake.<BR>You are the same decaying organic matter as everyone else."</I>||||reg||2
Z||000004||Tigger||12-04-2000||01:42 PM||||5 spokes, as a rule of thumb, look good on most Fieros, many members here like the TSR Blades, but I don't think those are available anymore.  16's are an overall affordable and good size.<P>I generally look for things like, are they going to be easy to clean and maintain?  Billet wheels look cool, but need to be polished every once in a while.  Wheels with a whole bunch of counterbored screws give the 3 piece wheel look, but could be a bear to clean.<P>Much of the choice depends on whether you want wheels for show or for every day driving.  For show you can go all out, for daily driving, look for wheels that will look good and easy to keep clean.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||RiceCooker||12-04-2000||03:09 PM|||| Gotta be 5x100 bolt pattern and stock is 35mm offest.<BR>I too have TSW blades and they are awesome.<BR>I was in the same boat as you are last year.<BR>My advice: Stick to 16's anything less and you'll want bigger, anything more and tires will cost you an arm and a leg. Yo have to shop around for a wheel that you like. There are computer programs (some even at wheel shops) that let you try out wheels on a car and even in many colors. They had one at Blaskin & Lane (might be only Canadian) and yes they even had fieros. Wheel/ tire shops are great places to shop but never buy from them. Their price markup is ridiculous. Once you find a set that you like, phone or e-mail the wheel company and they will help you out more because it is their product. I went to TSW because I loved the Blades and I heard they had great Customrer Service. I was not dissappointed.<P>Anything else?<P>Oh yeah, silver looks better than chrome on fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Greg Piet||12-04-2000||03:40 PM||||I like those teamloco 142 ones<BR>or the Kosei k1 racing wheels||||reg||1
